comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T22:04:51.089Z","harness:claude-code","pm-changelog half filed upstream as https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/issues/317 (render declared contract changes under Changed (SDK contract) with the migration line, mirror them in --changelog-json, and map them in pm changelog audit). The pm-cli half of this item is still unstarted: choose the declaration field on the closing item and add the release-time check against sdk/public-surface.json changes."
  "2026-11-06T04:55:55.428Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence for the release-time check (2026-11-06): pm-gh1663 changes the public SDK contract in the next Unreleased window. Before: GetResult.linked always carried files, tests and docs, and a nested selector padded unrequested groups with []. After: a nested selector (linked.files, claim_state.claimed) returns only the members it names, linked members are optional and claim_state is Partial; the omission receipt names populated siblings as <facet>.<member>. Migrate: read linked.<group> with optional chaining or ?? [], or request the whole linked selector. The sdk/public-surface.json acknowledgment carries the same line. Until this item ships, that acknowledgment and docs/GET_READ_EVIDENCE.md are the only migration record, because the changelog renders the item title under Fixed."
  "2026-11-08T00:39:15.975Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence for the release-time check (2026-11-08): pm-8s53lj and pm-hka7ep change the public SDK contract in the next Unreleased window. Before: comment, note and learning rows carried only their stored fields, a bounded comments or notes read kept the oldest rows, learnings had no output ceiling, and PmReadOutputCursorEnvelope continued forward only. After: every listing row leads with index (IndexedAnnotationEntry), the annotation command options accept expectAt for edit and delete, learnings joins PM_READ_OUTPUT_SURFACES, bounded annotation reads keep the newest rows and continue through a cursor with direction backward, and sliceReadOutputRowCollection takes an optional end. Migrate: address entries by row.index instead of array position, follow next_cursor for older entries, and accept the optional direction field when decoding cursors. The sdk/public-surface.json acknowledgment carries the same line.\n"
  "2026-11-08T02:52:23.427Z","harness:claude-code","Addendum (2026-11-08) to the pm-8s53lj contract line, from the PR 1685 review follow-up. Before: PmReadOutputSurfaceContract.budget_retention_policy was ordered_prefix or verdict_priority, and PmReadOutputTailRetentionPolicy declared only paths and total_key. After: comments, notes and learnings declare ordered_suffix, and a tail policy may declare delivered_row_counters (notes recount structured_event_count from the delivered rows); PmReadOutputDeliveredRowCounter is a new public type. Migrate: treat ordered_suffix as newest-first retention, and accept the optional delivered_row_counters field. The sdk/public-surface.json acknowledgment carries the same line.\n"
body: ""
